{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Thompson. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists on your care team. You're here today because of a kidney stone in your right ureter. We're going to get you ready for surgery tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, doctor. I’ve been having a lot of pain on my right side. Is that from the stone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s very likely. The stone is blocking the tube that carries urine from your kidney to your bladder, which causes pain and can affect kidney function if not treated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see. I’ve had stones before, but this one feels worse. What’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow you’ll have a procedure called ureteroscopy. The urologist will go in through your bladder and use a laser to break up the stone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds intense. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s very common and generally safe. But because you have a mechanical heart valve, we need to be careful with your blood thinners."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I take Coumadin every day. I stopped it as they told me, but I’m worried about clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. So we’re starting you on heparin today — an IV blood thinner — to protect your heart while we pause the Coumadin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. So I’m on heparin now instead?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Heparin works quickly and can be stopped right before surgery. After your procedure, we’ll restart Coumadin and overlap it with heparin until your INR is in the safe range — between 2.5 and 3.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. How long will I be here?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2191-01-18 11:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely about a week. We’ll keep you until we’re sure the Coumadin is working and you’re recovering well from surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2191-01-18 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I just reviewed your labs. Your hemoglobin is a bit low at 11.2, but stable. White blood cells are normal, so no sign of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2191-01-18 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the stone or something else?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2191-01-18 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Could be from minor bleeding related to the stone. You mentioned past guaiac-positive stools — we should keep an eye on that, but it’s not urgent now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2191-01-18 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. My breathing feels a little tight, but I think it’s just from being anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2191-01-18 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. You have COPD, so we’ll make sure your inhalers are available. Use your albuterol as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2191-01-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your PTT was checked this morning — it’s 51.3, which is in range for heparin. Surgery is scheduled for noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2191-01-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right? I’m nervous about the anesthesia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2191-01-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very normal to feel that way. The anesthesiologist will use general anesthesia, but they’ll monitor your heart and lungs closely. Your history of heart attack and COPD means extra caution, but you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2191-01-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had two strokes and heart surgery — I just want to get through this safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2191-01-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And that’s exactly our goal. Your team knows your history well. We’ve coordinated with cardiology and anesthesia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2191-01-19 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, Mr. Thompson. You’re back from surgery. Everything went smoothly — the stone was broken up and a stent was placed in your ureter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2191-01-19 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, thank goodness. I feel groggy, but no pain yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2191-01-19 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. You’ll likely feel some flank discomfort or urgency to urinate because of the stent, but we’ll manage that with pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2191-01-19 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2191-01-19 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We need to restart your Coumadin and make sure your INR climbs into the target range. That’ll take a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2191-01-19 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your post-op PTT came back at 97.7 — a bit high, but expected after heparin. We’ve adjusted the drip to keep it safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2191-01-19 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? High PTT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2191-01-19 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We monitor it closely. Right now, it’s within acceptable limits for your situation. We’re balancing bleeding risk with clot prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2191-01-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was 163 yesterday — a bit high, but not concerning. We’ll keep monitoring it. Are you taking your diabetes meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2191-01-20 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been on glyburide and metformin for years. I try to watch my diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2191-01-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re continuing those here. Your kidney function is normal — creatinine is 0.9 — so it’s safe to keep using them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2191-01-20 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I’ve been urinating a little pink. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2191-01-20 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, light pink urine is common after this procedure. It’s from minor bleeding due to the stent. As long as it’s not bright red or clotted, it’s okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2191-01-20 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2191-01-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.1. We’re getting closer to the target of 2.5–3.5. We’ll keep the heparin running a bit longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2191-01-21 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So once it hits 2.5, I can stop the IV and go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2191-01-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Almost. We’ll stop heparin when your INR is stable above 2.5. Then we’ll observe you for a day to make sure it stays up before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2191-01-21 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been constipated since the surgery. Is that from the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2191-01-21 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very likely. Narcotics can slow your bowels. We’ll start docusate, a stool softener, to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2191-01-21 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I don’t want to be uncomfortable longer than I have to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2191-01-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news — your INR is 2.8 today. That’s in the target range. We’re stopping the heparin now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2191-01-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2191-01-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll watch your INR tomorrow to confirm it stays stable. If so, discharge is likely on the 25th."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2191-01-22 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have a question about my Coumadin. I was taking 8mg most days, but 6mg on Tuesdays and Fridays. Should I go back to that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2191-01-22 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We recommend resuming your home schedule: 8mg daily except Tuesdays and Fridays when you take 6mg. Your PCP or Coumadin nurse will monitor your INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2191-01-22 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried I’d forget."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2191-01-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR held at 2.7 today — stable. You’re on track for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2191-01-23 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about the stent? When does that come out?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2191-01-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urologist will schedule that as an outpatient procedure in a week or two. It’s quick and done with a scope."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2191-01-23 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking my heart and blood pressure meds here — metoprolol, ramipril, furosemide. Should I keep those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2191-01-23 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, resume all your home medications. You have diastolic heart failure and hypertension, so those are important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2191-01-23 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my cholesterol meds — atorvastatin and ezetimibe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2191-01-23 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue those. You have coronary disease, so keeping your LDL low is key."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2191-01-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’ll get a prescription for oxycodone for pain, but use it sparingly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2191-01-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t like taking narcotics. Can I switch to something else?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2191-01-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. Talk to your PCP about alternatives. Just don’t drive or drink alcohol while on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2191-01-24 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What signs should I watch for after I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2191-01-24 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor if you develop fever over 101.5, vomiting, or severe pain. Also watch for heavy bleeding or signs of clot — like chest pain or weakness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2191-01-24 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2191-01-24 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your PCP within three days to check your INR. And schedule with your urologist for stent removal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re medically cleared to go home. I’ve reviewed everything with you — any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I understand. Resume all my meds, watch for fever, and see my doctors soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You did well. Take care, and call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing — my feet have been itchy. Should I use that lotion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the camphor-menthol lotion is for your chronic skin condition. Use it as needed for itching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're all set. The nurse will bring your discharge papers shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Thompson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Remember, call if you have chest pain — use the nitroglycerin and call 911."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I keep it with me always."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll use the inhalers if I get short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re well prepared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for making sure I understood everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s our job. Get some rest and take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe journey home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2191-01-25 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2191-01-18 11:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2191-01-25 11:44:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. Thompson was admitted for a right ureteral stone requiring surgical intervention. Given his mechanical aortic valve and chronic anticoagulation with Coumadin, he was admitted early for a heparin bridge. He underwent right ureteroscopy with laser lithotripsy and stent placement on January 19 without complications. Postoperatively, he was transitioned back to Coumadin with overlapping heparin until his INR reached the therapeutic range of 2.5–3.5. His hospital course was uncomplicated, with stable management of comorbidities including diastolic heart failure, COPD, diabetes, and coronary artery disease. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with his PCP for INR monitoring and urology for stent removal.",
    "problems": [
      "Calculus of ureter",
      "Diastolic heart failure, unspecified",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia"
    ]
  }
}
